## Layered architecture and falsification plan

These are sensory hypotheses to test, not predicted observations or evaporation results.

| Window | Intended relationship | Failure that rejects the candidate |
|---|---|---|
| Opening, 0–5 min | Bergamot/citrus and restrained cassis against already present dry woody/mineral context; pineapple recognizable only as an accent | Tropical juice/candy takes over; cassis reads as berry syrup; wood/ambergris absent; harsh green ester |
| Heart, 30 min | Transparent floral/pepper bridge retains space between citrus memory, pineapple trace and cedar/patchouli | Fruit becomes the main object, or a hollow gap appears between top and base |
| Late heart, 2 h | Dry woods, Ambrox, patchouli and musk sustain continuity; trace leather/smoke acts as a transition | Generic amberwood, metallic laundry, scratchy mineral overload or smoky tar dominates |
| Drydown, 4 h and next day if present | Dry woody/ambergris-like chypre return with musk; fruit subordinate | Residual fruit overwhelms the structure, Ambrox is harsh, or drydown is unlike the selected Aventus reference |

Do not “repair” any low modeled fruit OAV by automatically adding pineapple. The user's prior fruit-overload report is a reason to test a smaller fruit allowance even if a numeric model predicts it will be weak. Conversely, a trace mass does not prove that a potent odorant is quiet.

After stock and safety prerequisites are met, compare blinded complete-batch AAG arms at 0.5x, 1.0x and 1.5x of the **0.015 g active reference target**, keeping every other aromatic dose fixed. Match non-ethanol carriers across arms using verified blank carriers, then adjust final ethanol by mass to a constant finished mass. Explicitly record the ethanol replacement and the small change in total aromatic mass; these are not all exactly 20% w/w. Do not compensate with extra Iso E Super, Hedione or musk. Assess alongside one identified authentic reference bottle and a repeated coded control, randomized over separate sessions.

Only after the fruit question is resolved, test the Ambrox level in a separate controlled series, matching its DPG/IPM carriers and recording ethanol compensation. Then test the musk alternative or omission in its own series. No multi-musk stack is justified by this model. Any omission is a falsification probe, not an automatically promoted improved formula. Record reference identity, stock/lot IDs, mass, matrix, temperature, rest time, order, evaluator and scores for fruit intrusion, woody/mineral identity, bridge continuity, harshness and overall reference likeness. Similarity and liking remain separate questions.

## Pipeline Analysis

**NOT RUN — this is an incomplete gravimetric design, not an executable volumetric formula.** The existing release CLI consumes microlitre formula tables. No fictitious density, unknown stock basis or single-molecule natural ODT was supplied to generate a headspace report.

ODT, OAV, vapor ppm, temporal headspace, note-distribution percentages, evaporation, sillage, skin longevity, IFRA clearance and release status are **UNKNOWN / NOT TESTED**, not zero. Concentrate ppm must use the full stock-blend mass once known; the aromatic-basis and finished-batch target ppm above are explicitly different denominators.

For a later executable child: reread inventory, resolve basis/carrier/grade and matrix inputs, preserve active mass under stock changes, identify the actual immediate parent, run the existing release gate with active-dose and OAV-per-time checks, and present its full formatted headspace/temporal/perfumer analysis both in chat and in that child file. Pipeline bounds or OAV cannot certify the sensory architecture.

